<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aschersleben</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aschersleben is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the northern edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harz">Harz</a>. It is one of the oldest towns in the region, and its name in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>, Ascharia, gave the Ascanian dynasty, the ruling family of Anhalt, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> and Saxony-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a>, its name. After a branch of the family died out in 1315 the town passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halberstadt">Halberstadt</a>, and later to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-prussia">Brandenburg-Prussia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aschersleben.jpg" alt="Aschersleben" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: I. Diron · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rondellblick.ASL.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
